course: dictionary
lesson: 12242
title: Consonantal
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A consonant is a sound you make by blocking the air a little with your lips, tongue or teeth. Say b, t, m and s slowly and you can feel the air being stopped or squeezed. Consonantal means to do with consonants.
explain: «The consonantal cluster str starts the word street.» Vowels, like a, e, i, o and u, are open sounds where the air flows freely. A word with many consonant sounds packed together is full of blocked sounds.
explain: Look at the ending. Words ending in -al often mean "relating to", so consonantal means relating to consonants. If you can say "to do with consonants" in your sentence and it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Consonants are sounds like b, t, m and s, made by blocking the air with lips, tongue or teeth.
fact: Vowels are open sounds, like a, e, i, o and u in most words.
fact: «Consonantal cluster» means several consonants together, like «str» in «street».
fact: «Consonantal» means to do with consonants, or made of consonants.
fact: Some writing systems, such as Hebrew and Arabic, are consonantal: they mostly write only consonants.
exercise: «The word street begins with a consonantal cluster.» What does consonantal mean here? | To do with the sea | Very loud | *To do with consonants | A long, slow word
exercise: Which sound is a consonant? | a | *m | u | e
exercise: Which of these is a consonantal writing system, mostly written with consonants? | Road signs | Music notes | *Hebrew
test: Which sound is an open sound, not a consonant? | *a | b | s | t
test: Consonantal means: | A type of loud music | To do with counting words | *To do with consonants | To do with vowels only
exam: Which word begins with a consonantal cluster? | apple | tea | *strong | ice
